A||||4||fiero87||New Intake Design??||||5||
Z||000000||fiero87||09-29-2000||11:40 AM||||Hello fellow fourm members,<P>I was thinking the other day after looking through my big book of fiero parts, and wondering what would be the best design of an intkae for 2.8 V-6?  A lot of my friends drive imports and they have the open element filters at the end of a pipe.  Is this something to look into?  I also thought about adding a rear decklid scoop(lower profile, not ricer, or indy style).  Would there be any benifit to rigging the intake to this?  Or is the stock intake sufficant??  I'm going to be adding a bored out throtle body soon, so i want to feed it as much cold air as possible.  Any idea's?  Thanks<BR>Tim||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cooter||09-29-2000||01:25 PM||||I have an Indy scoop with large K/N filter stuck in it on my 3.4- I also have a big bore throttle body. I drove the car for a while with the stock air box and throttle body before making the swap. After adding the goodies, I noticed:<BR>There is a really neat noise in the scoop when you open the throttle. Throttle response with the bigger bore is weird. It has all kinds of response from idle to half throttle, but above half throttle it really doesnt change much. To me, that means that the engine is not able to move enough air for the throttle body to be a restriction. But I got it done for me for free, so no big deal.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-29-2000||02:00 PM||||the air duct is a non issue as far as flow. letting heat out of the engine bay will help by keeping the intake hardware cooler. that always helps. just how much is hard to say.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ThatRickGuy||09-29-2000||03:25 PM||||I've been toying with the idea of designin a scoop system from the Fi-Air-O scoops, I think they look better then the indy scoop, and also, with Chris West's dual throttle body design you could run two seperate intake systems. then it becomes a matter of helping the engine breath... borla exhaust, headers, or at least opening up the manifolds, port matching everything, 1.6 rockers, wild cam and if possible, enlarging the valves. And just for some added heat protection, get one of those rearward facing scoops for the decklid, and those larger side air scoops, but just have them open in the back so cold air gets pushed into the engine bay. Now if I just had a couple thousand dollars to actually do it... heheheh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||09-29-2000||08:39 PM||||You don't want the TB's breathing air thru diferant plumbing paths. It sounds like a good idea but you can end up with flow ballance problems very easily.||||reg||1
